NNAAMMEE
     ttsseecc — Freescale Three-Speed Ethernet Controller device driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ttsseecc
           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ttsseecc driver provides support for the gigabit Ethernet controller in‐
     tegrated in some of the Freescale system-on-chip devices.

     The ttsseecc driver supports the following media types:

     autoselect            Enable autoselection of the media type and options

     10baseT/UTP           Set 10Mbps operation

     100baseTX             Set 100Mbps operation

     1000baseT             Set 1000baseT operation

     The ttsseecc driver supports the following media options:

     full-duplex           Set full duplex operation

     The ttsseecc driver supports polled operation when the system is configured
     with DEVICE_POLLING kernel option, see polling(4) for more details.

     The ttsseecc driver supports reception and transmission of extended frames
     for vlan(4).  This capability of ttsseecc can be controlled by means of the
     vvllaannmmttuu parameter to ifconfig(8).

     The ttsseecc driver supports interrupts coalescing (IC) so that raising a
     transmit/receive frame interrupt is delayed, if possible, until a thresh‐
     old-defined period of time has elapsed, or a threshold-defined frame
     counter has been reached (whichever occurs first).  The following sysctls
     regulate this behaviour:

     _d_e_v_._t_s_e_c_._X_._i_n_t___c_o_a_l_._r_x___t_i_m_e

     _d_e_v_._t_s_e_c_._X_._i_n_t___c_o_a_l_._r_x___c_o_u_n_t

     _d_e_v_._t_s_e_c_._X_._i_n_t___c_o_a_l_._t_x___t_i_m_e

     _d_e_v_._t_s_e_c_._X_._i_n_t___c_o_a_l_._t_x___c_o_u_n_t

             Value of 0 for either time or count disables IC on the given
             path.  Time value 1-65535 corresponds to a real time period and
             is expressed in units equivalent to 64 ticks of the TSEC clock.
             Count 1-255 represents the number of frames (note that value of 1
             is equivalent to IC disabled).  User provided values larger than
             supported will be trimmed to the maximum supported.  More details
             are available in the reference manual of the device.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     Gigabit Ethernet controllers built into the following Freescale system-
     on-chip devices are known to work with the ttsseecc driver:

     ••   MPC8349
     ••   MPC8533, MPC8541, MPC8555

     The enhanced version of the controller (eTSEC), integrated in the follow‐
     ing devices, is also supported by this driver:

     ••   MPC8548, MPC8572

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     altq(4), arp(4), miibus(4), netintro(4), ng_ether(4), polling(4),
     vlan(4), ifconfig(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ttsseecc device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 8.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The base version of ttsseecc device driver was written by Piotr Kruszynski.
     It has been extended with polling and interrupt coalescing support by
     Rafal Jaworowski.  It has been further enhanced with multicast, h/w
     checksum calculation and vlan support by Piotr Ziecik.  This manual page
     was written by Rafal Jaworowski.

